  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal Express obligated $346M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Federal Express received 912 awards year to date, with an average award size of $379K, and obligations were down 40.5% year over year. Federal Express obligations by fiscal year show a peak in FY24 at $677M, followed by $582M in FY25 and $346M in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is Federal Express's largest buyer in FY2026 to date, with $193M obligated, followed by the Department of Defense with $135M. Couriers and Express Delivery Services is the dominant market for Federal Express, accounting for $345M of obligations in FY2026 to date. Federal Express also shows activity in Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation at $1.5M. Current-year totals are partial, representing fiscal year to date activity for Federal Express.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Federal Express obligations changed year over year?",
        "body": "Federal Express obligations fell 40.5% year over year. Federal Express obligated $346M in FY2026 to date, down from $582M in FY25 and $677M in FY24. Federal Express obligations earlier in the decade included $305M in FY21, $309M in FY22, and $275M in FY23."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Federal Express's biggest federal customers in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is Federal Express's largest buyer at $193M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense follows with $135M, then the Department of Justice at $7.2M and the Department of Transportation at $3.6M."
      }
    ]
